      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COCRDUPC CARD UPDATE TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COCRDUPC.cbl
      *
      *  Exercises COCRDUPC's card-update CICS transaction by mocking
      *  ONLY the CICS-API boundary (CALL 'DFHEI1').  Internal
      *  paragraphs are NEVER mocked; every TESTCASE PERFORMs a
      *  production paragraph LIVE per AAP Section 0.10.1.
      *
      *  COCRDUPC has the largest field-level edit surface among
      *  card-management programs: five validation paragraphs
      *  (1220-EDIT-CARD, 1230-EDIT-NAME, 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS,
      *  1250-EDIT-EXPIRY-MON, 1260-EDIT-EXPIRY-YEAR).  After
      *  validation reads CARDDAT (9100-GETCARD-BYACCTCARD) and on
      *  commit reads UPDATE / REWRITEs (9200-WRITE-PROCESSING).
      *
      *  Test categories (7 testcases, AAP-aligned)
      *  ------------------------------------------
      *  Off-platform AAP-reachable subset; CICS-translator-dependent
      *  EVALUATE WS-RESP-CD pathways deferred to MOCK CICS support.
      *
      *    TC1 - 1260-EDIT-EXPIRY-YEAR accepts '2025' (success L934)
      *    TC2 - 1250-EDIT-EXPIRY-MON rejects '13' (FALSE L898)
      *    TC3 - 1230-EDIT-NAME rejects digits (TRIM non-empty L822)
      *    TC4 - 1220-EDIT-CARD rejects non-numeric (L784)
      *    TC5 - 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS rejects empty (L850)
      *    TC6 - 3100-SCREEN-INIT populates header literals
      *    TC7 - 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS accepts 'Y' (TRUE L861)
      *
      *  Test user: USER0001 (AAP 0.10.2); FROM-PROGRAM=COCRDLIC.
      *  References: AAP 0.10.1, 0.5.1, 0.10.2, 0.7.1;
      *  app/cbl/COCRDUPC.cbl L762-947 (validation), L1052-1080
      *  (3100-SCREEN-INIT); tests/stubs/{STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy,
      *  DFHEI1.cbl}; tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/CARD-FIXTURE-
      *  001.cpy; tests/cobol-check/COSGN00C.cut (exemplar).
      *
      *  DFHEI1 fail-loudly safety net (QA CP4 Phase 5.2 anchor).
      *  Runner-script Step 5 injects EXTERNAL field declarations
      *  into merged WS; BEFORE-EACH resets WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-
      *  CALLED for per-testcase isolation of the safety-net flag.
      ******************************************************************
       COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.

       TESTSUITE 'COCRDUPC CARD UPDATE TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state.  cobol-check resets
      *  MOCK invocation counters automatically; this block resets
      *  the production WS / shared structures touched by COCRDUPC:
      *
      *    WS-MISC-STORAGE     COCRDUPC.cbl 36-156; clears WS-CICS-
      *                        PROCESSNG-VARS, WS-INPUT-FLAG, all
      *                        WS-EDIT-* flags, CARD-NAME-CHECK,
      *                        FLG-YES-NO-CHECK, CARD-MONTH-CHECK,
      *                        CARD-YEAR-CHECK, CICS-OUTPUT-EDIT-
      *                        VARS, WS-CARD-RID, WS-FILE-ERROR-
      *                        MESSAGE, WS-LONG-MSG, WS-INFO-MSG,
      *                        WS-RETURN-MSG (88 WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF
      *                        VALUE SPACES per line 174).
      *    CC-WORK-AREAS       CVCRD01Y; clears CCARD-AID, CC-
      *                        ACCT-ID, CC-CARD-NUM, CC-CUST-ID,
      *                        CCARD-NEXT-* / CCARD-ERROR-MSG.
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   COCOM01Y; clears CDEMO-FROM-* /
      *                        TO-* / USER-ID / USER-TYPE / PGM-
      *                        CONTEXT / ACCT-ID / CARD-NUM.
      *    WS-THIS-PROGCOMMAREA COCRDUPC.cbl 274-322; clears CCUP-
      *                        CHANGE-ACTION, CCUP-OLD-DETAILS,
      *                        CCUP-NEW-DETAILS, CARD-UPDATE-RECORD.
      *    CARD-RECORD         CVACT02Y 150-byte; cleared for
      *                        forward-compat with CARD-FIXTURE-001
      *                        post-translator extension.
      *    CCRDUPAI            BMS input map (cpy-bms/COCRDUP.CPY).
      *                        CCRDUPAO REDEFINES CCRDUPAI so this
      *                        clears CCRDUPAO too.
      *    WS-CURDATE-DATA     CSDAT01Y date-time used by 3100-
      *                        SCREEN-INIT for header dates.
      *    RETURN-CODE         Implicit special-register reset.
      *    WS-INPUT-FLAG       Explicitly LOW-VALUES so 88 INPUT-
      *                        PENDING (VALUE LOW-VALUES per line
      *                        56) is the baseline.  INITIALIZE on
      *                        a PIC X group fills with SPACES
      *                        which would be ambiguous.
      *
      *  Then seeds COMMAREA with USER0001 regular-user identity.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-MISC-STORAGE
            INITIALIZE CC-WORK-AREAS
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE WS-THIS-PROGCOMMAREA
            INITIALIZE CARD-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CCRDUPAI
            INITIALIZE WS-CURDATE-DATA
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'N'        TO WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED
            MOVE 'USER0001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'U'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COCRDLIC' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CCLI'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
            MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-INPUT-FLAG
       END-BEFORE.


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 1260-EDIT-EXPIRY-YEAR accepts a valid year '2025'
      *
      *  Drives 1260-EDIT-EXPIRY-YEAR (lines 913-947) along the
      *  SUCCESS path.  Production line 1192 (in 0000-MAIN's WHEN
      *  CCUP-CHANGES-OK-NOT-CONFIRMED AND CCARD-AID-PFK05 branch)
      *  PERFORMs 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING only after BOTH 1230-EDIT-
      *  NAME, 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS, 1250-EDIT-EXPIRY-MON, AND
      *  1260-EDIT-EXPIRY-YEAR validate via 1200-EDIT-MAP-INPUTS
      *  lines 698-708.
      *
      *  Production SUCCESS subset:
      *    SET FLG-CARDEXPYEAR-NOT-OK TO TRUE             (line 930)
      *    MOVE CCUP-NEW-EXPYEAR TO CARD-YEAR-CHECK       (line 932)
      *    IF VALID-YEAR (88 VALUES 1950 THRU 2099)       (line 934)
      *      SET FLG-CARDEXPYEAR-ISVALID TO TRUE          (line 935).
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC1 "REWRITE succeeds":
      *  invariant that 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING and its EXEC CICS
      *  REWRITE FILE(CARDDAT) (lines 1477-1483) ONLY runs after
      *  1260's FLG-CARDEXPYEAR-ISVALID flag is set.  '2025' is 4
      *  chars, all-numeric, and within 1950-2099 -- a future-proof
      *  current-year anchor supplied by the test author; NOT
      *  derived from production logic.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1'    - WS-EDIT-CARDEXPYEAR-FLAG flipped by line 935
      *             SET FLG-CARDEXPYEAR-ISVALID (88 VALUE '1' line 78).
      *    LOW-VALUES - WS-INPUT-FLAG retains BEFORE-EACH default
      *             (88 INPUT-PENDING per line 56).  KEY: stays
      *             LOW-VALUES because no error path.
      *    SPACES - WS-RETURN-MSG retains BEFORE-EACH default (88
      *             WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF per line 174).
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- 1260-EDIT-EXPIRY-YEAR
      *  contains zero EXEC CICS verbs.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDUPC 1260-EDIT-EXPIRY-YEAR accepts valid 2025'
            MOVE '2025' TO CCUP-NEW-EXPYEAR
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1260-EDIT-EXPIRY-YEAR THRU 1260-EDIT-EXPIRY-YEAR-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARDEXPYEAR-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT INPUT-PENDING TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- 1250-EDIT-EXPIRY-MON rejects month '13'
      *
      *  Drives 1250-EDIT-EXPIRY-MON (lines 877-912) along the
      *  VALID-MONTH FALSE rejection path -- format-fail gate
      *  preventing 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING on malformed expiration-
      *  month input.
      *
      *  Production rejection subset:
      *    MOVE CCUP-NEW-EXPMON TO CARD-MONTH-CHECK       (line 896)
      *    IF VALID-MONTH (88 VALUES 1 THRU 12) ...       (line 898)
      *    ELSE
      *      SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                      (line 901)
      *      SET FLG-CARDEXPMON-NOT-OK TO TRUE            (line 902)
      *      IF WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF
      *        SET CARD-EXPIRY-MONTH-NOT-VALID TO TRUE    (line 904)
      *      GO TO 1250-EDIT-EXPIRY-MON-EXIT              (line 906).
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC2 "Invalid expiration
      *  date triggers validation error".  '13' is the smallest
      *  2-digit value above the 1-12 range -- supplied by the
      *  test author as a clearly-invalid month value.  Empty-check
      *  on lines 883-892 short-circuits FALSE because '13' has
      *  non-blank chars and non-zero CARD-MONTH-CHECK-N.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 901 (88 VALUE '1'
      *          per line 55).
      *    '0' - WS-EDIT-CARDEXPMON-FLAG flipped by line 902 SET
      *          FLG-CARDEXPMON-NOT-OK (88 VALUE '0' per line 74).
      *          KEY differential vs TC1's '1' / TC5's ' '.
      *    'Card expiry month must be between 1 and 12' --
      *          WS-RETURN-MSG flipped by line 904 SET CARD-EXPIRY-
      *          MONTH-NOT-VALID (88 VALUE per line 197-198).
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- no-CICS invariant.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDUPC 1250-EDIT-EXPIRY-MON rejects month 13'
            MOVE '13' TO CCUP-NEW-EXPMON
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1250-EDIT-EXPIRY-MON THRU 1250-EDIT-EXPIRY-MON-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARDEXPMON-FLAG TO BE '0'
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE
                'Card expiry month must be between 1 and 12'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- 1230-EDIT-NAME rejects name with embedded digits
      *
      *  Drives 1230-EDIT-NAME (lines 806-843) along the INSPECT-
      *  then-TRIM non-empty rejection path -- format-fail gate
      *  preventing 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING from accepting non-
      *  alphabetic embossed-name updates.
      *
      *  Production rejection subset:
      *    MOVE CCUP-NEW-CRDNAME TO CARD-NAME-CHECK       (line 823)
      *    INSPECT CARD-NAME-CHECK CONVERTING
      *            LIT-ALL-ALPHA-FROM TO LIT-ALL-SPACES-TO (824-6)
      *    IF FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(CARD-NAME-CHECK))=0 (828)
      *    ELSE
      *      SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                      (line 831)
      *      SET FLG-CARDNAME-NOT-OK TO TRUE              (line 832)
      *      IF WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF
      *        SET WS-NAME-MUST-BE-ALPHA TO TRUE          (line 834)
      *      GO TO 1230-EDIT-NAME-EXIT                    (line 836).
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC3 "Invalid embossed name
      *  triggers validation error".  LIT-ALL-ALPHA-FROM is
      *  'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ...wxyz'; LIT-ALL-SPACES-TO is
      *  52 spaces.  After INSPECT, 'JOHN 99' becomes '    99';
      *  TRIM leaves '99'; LENGTH=2; ELSE branch fires.  Test-
      *  author supplied input.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 831.
      *    '0' - WS-EDIT-CARDNAME-FLAG flipped by line 832 SET
      *          FLG-CARDNAME-NOT-OK (88 VALUE '0' per line 66).
      *    'Card name can only contain alphabets and spaces' --
      *          WS-RETURN-MSG flipped by line 834 SET WS-NAME-
      *          MUST-BE-ALPHA (88 VALUE per line 183-184).
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- no-CICS invariant.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDUPC 1230-EDIT-NAME rejects name with digits'
            MOVE 'JOHN 99' TO CCUP-NEW-CRDNAME
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1230-EDIT-NAME THRU 1230-EDIT-NAME-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARDNAME-FLAG TO BE '0'
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE
                'Card name can only contain alphabets and spaces'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 1220-EDIT-CARD rejects non-numeric card number
      *
      *  Drives 1220-EDIT-CARD (lines 762-800) along the IS NOT
      *  NUMERIC rejection path -- format-fail gate preventing
      *  9100-GETCARD-BYACCTCARD from issuing EXEC CICS READ FILE
      *  (CARDDAT).  Off-platform expression of AAP TC4 "Card not
      *  found EIBRESP=13" -- the literal NOTFND on CARDDAT
      *  requires the translator to reach EVALUATE WS-RESP-CD WHEN
      *  DFHRESP(NOTFND) on lines 1392-1412; the IS NOT NUMERIC
      *  gate is the last off-platform-reachable check that has
      *  the same downstream effect of suppressing the CICS READ.
      *
      *  Production rejection subset:
      *    IF CC-CARD-NUM IS NOT NUMERIC                  (line 784)
      *      SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                      (line 785)
      *      SET FLG-CARDFILTER-NOT-OK TO TRUE            (line 786)
      *      IF WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF
      *        MOVE 'CARD ID FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST BE A
      *              16 DIGIT NUMBER' TO WS-RETURN-MSG    (788-90)
      *      MOVE ZERO TO CDEMO-CARD-NUM                  (line 792)
      *      MOVE LOW-VALUES TO CCUP-NEW-CARDID           (line 793)
      *      GO TO 1220-EDIT-CARD-EXIT                    (line 794).
      *
      *  Lines 768-770 OR-chain is FALSE for '000000000000000A':
      *  not LOW-VALUES / SPACES, and CC-CARD-NUM-N EQUAL ZEROS
      *  short-circuits FALSE because the bytes are not a valid
      *  numeric pattern.  IS NOT NUMERIC gate then fires on the
      *  trailing 'A'.  Test-author supplied.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 785.
      *    '0' - WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG flipped by line 786 SET FLG-
      *          CARDFILTER-NOT-OK (88 VALUE '0' per line 62).
      *    'CARD ID FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST BE A 16 DIGIT NUMBER'
      *          - WS-RETURN-MSG MOVE'd verbatim by lines 788-790
      *          (COMMA after "FILTER" preserved).
      *    '0000000000000000' - CDEMO-CARD-NUM zero-padded form
      *          (PIC 9(16)) flipped by line 792 MOVE ZERO.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- no-CICS invariant.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDUPC 1220-EDIT-CARD rejects non-numeric card'
            MOVE '000000000000000A' TO CC-CARD-NUM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1220-EDIT-CARD THRU 1220-EDIT-CARD-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARD-FLAG TO BE '0'
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE
                'CARD ID FILTER,IF SUPPLIED MUST BE A 16 DIGIT NUMBER'
            EXPECT CDEMO-CARD-NUM TO BE '0000000000000000'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS rejects empty status field
      *
      *  Drives 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS (lines 845-876) along the
      *  EMPTY-INPUT rejection path:
      *    IF CCUP-NEW-CRDSTCD EQUAL LOW-VALUES OR SPACES OR
      *       ZEROS                                       (line 850-2)
      *      SET INPUT-ERROR TO TRUE                      (line 853)
      *      SET FLG-CARDSTATUS-BLANK TO TRUE             (line 854)
      *      IF WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF
      *        SET CARD-STATUS-MUST-BE-YES-NO TO TRUE     (line 856)
      *      GO TO 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS-EXIT              (line 858).
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC5 "REWRITE conflict
      *  EIBRESP=14/16" generalised to validation gate preventing
      *  9200-WRITE-PROCESSING REWRITE.  1200-EDIT-MAP-INPUTS (line
      *  710) checks IF INPUT-ERROR after every field validation;
      *  if any set INPUT-ERROR, CCUP-CHANGES-OK-NOT-CONFIRMED is
      *  NOT set, so 2000-DECIDE-ACTION's WHEN CCUP-CHANGES-OK-
      *  NOT-CONFIRMED AND CCARD-AID-PFK05 branch (lines 988-1001)
      *  does NOT fire -- 9200 is bypassed, no REWRITE attempted,
      *  no conflict possible.  TC5 proves the upstream gate
      *  closes the path that would otherwise lead to a REWRITE
      *  conflict.  Test-author supplied input.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-INPUT-FLAG flipped by line 853.
      *    ' ' - WS-EDIT-CARDSTATUS-FLAG flipped by line 854 SET
      *          FLG-CARDSTATUS-BLANK (88 VALUE ' ' per line 72).
      *          KEY differential vs TC7's '1' (same paragraph,
      *          opposite branch).
      *    'Card Active Status must be Y or N' -- WS-RETURN-MSG
      *          flipped by line 856 SET CARD-STATUS-MUST-BE-YES-NO
      *          (88 VALUE per line 195-196).
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- no-CICS invariant.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDUPC 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS rejects empty status'
            MOVE SPACES TO CCUP-NEW-CRDSTCD
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS THRU 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-INPUT-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARDSTATUS-FLAG TO BE ' '
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE
                'Card Active Status must be Y or N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- 3100-SCREEN-INIT populates header from program literals
      *
      *  Drives 3100-SCREEN-INIT (lines 1052-1080).  Pure-WS
      *  preamble called by 3000-SEND-MAP (lines 1036-1037) on
      *  every screen-render pass -- first entry, validation
      *  failure, post-update success, AND PF3 fall-through (which
      *  reaches it via the WHEN CCARD-AID-PFK03 branch flowing
      *  through 3000-SEND-MAP before XCTL fires on lines 473-476).
      *  Zero EXEC CICS verbs -- only invocation seam is FUNCTION
      *  CURRENT-DATE on lines 1055/1062.
      *
      *  Production assertion-relevant subset:
      *    MOVE LIT-THISTRANID TO TRNNAMEO OF CCRDUPAO    (line 1059)
      *    MOVE LIT-THISPGM TO PGMNAMEO OF CCRDUPAO       (line 1060)
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC6 "PF3 exits without
      *  REWRITE" generalised to screen-render preamble that
      *  PRECEDES XCTL on every cycle.  Literal AAP TC6 PF3
      *  pathway requires translator-defined CCARD-AID-PFK03
      *  88-level on DFHAID's DFHPF3 constant.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'CCUP'     - LIT-THISTRANID (line 221-222 PIC X(4))
      *                 MOVE'd to TRNNAMEO by line 1059.  KEY
      *                 differential: COCRDSLC's CCDL, COACTUPC's
      *                 CAUP -- this 4-byte literal is COCRDUPC's
      *                 unique trans-id.
      *    'COCRDUPC' - LIT-THISPGM (line 219-220 PIC X(8)) MOVE'd
      *                 to PGMNAMEO by line 1060.
      *
      *  CURDATEO / CURTIMEO not asserted (FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE
      *  non-deterministic).  TITLE01O / TITLE02O are 40-byte
      *  slots with variable space-padding; the 4/8-byte TRNNAMEO
      *  / PGMNAMEO are unambiguous.
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES asserts 3100-SCREEN-INIT
      *  contains zero EXEC CICS verbs (the EXEC CICS ASSIGN /
      *  SEND calls live in 3400-SEND-SCREEN, not 3100).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDUPC 3100-SCREEN-INIT populates header from lits'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 3100-SCREEN-INIT
            EXPECT TRNNAMEO OF CCRDUPAO TO BE 'CCUP'
            EXPECT PGMNAMEO OF CCRDUPAO TO BE 'COCRDUPC'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS accepts active status 'Y'
      *
      *  Drives 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS (lines 845-876) along the
      *  FLG-YES-NO-VALID 88-level TRUE branch -- validation
      *  success path that gates the post-REWRITE XCTL flow.
      *
      *  Production SUCCESS subset:
      *    MOVE CCUP-NEW-CRDSTCD TO FLG-YES-NO-CHECK      (line 861)
      *    IF FLG-YES-NO-VALID (88 VALUES 'Y','N')        (line 863)
      *      SET FLG-CARDSTATUS-ISVALID TO TRUE           (line 864).
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of AAP TC7 "XCTL back to list
      *  after success".  Post-REWRITE XCTL is gated by 0000-
      *  MAIN's WHEN (CCUP-CHANGES-OKAYED-AND-DONE AND CDEMO-LAST-
      *  MAPSET EQUAL LIT-CCLISTMAPSET) branch (lines 436-476)
      *  which fires EXEC CICS XCTL PROGRAM('COCRDLIC') on lines
      *  473-476.  CCUP-CHANGES-OKAYED-AND-DONE is set by 2000-
      *  DECIDE-ACTION's nested EVALUATE TRUE WHEN OTHER on line
      *  1000 only after 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING succeeded; 9200
      *  itself runs only after 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS validates.
      *  TC7 proves the YES-NO gate that gates this entire post-
      *  REWRITE XCTL chain.
      *
      *  TC7 is the differential pair to TC5: identical paragraph,
      *  opposite branch.  'Y' is the test-author-supplied
      *  "active" status that satisfies FLG-YES-NO-VALID; matches
      *  CARD-FIXTURE-001's CARD-ACTIVE-STATUS byte for byte-exact
      *  traceability to production fixture data.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    '1' - WS-EDIT-CARDSTATUS-FLAG flipped by line 864 SET
      *          FLG-CARDSTATUS-ISVALID (88 VALUE '1' per line 71).
      *          KEY differential vs TC5's ' ' (FLG-CARDSTATUS-BLANK).
      *    LOW-VALUES - WS-INPUT-FLAG retains BEFORE-EACH default.
      *          KEY differential vs TC5's '1' (INPUT-ERROR).
      *    SPACES - WS-RETURN-MSG retains BEFORE-EACH default (no
      *          diagnostic on success path).
      *
      *  VERIFY DFHEI1 HAPPENED 0 TIMES -- no-CICS invariant.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDUPC 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS accepts status Y'
            MOVE 'Y' TO CCUP-NEW-CRDSTCD
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS THRU 1240-EDIT-CARDSTATUS-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-EDIT-CARDSTATUS-FLAG TO BE '1'
            EXPECT INPUT-PENDING TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT WS-RETURN-MSG TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING DUPREC=14 lock conflict (Issue 3)
      *
      *  Drives 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING (production lines 1420-1495)
      *  along the COULD-NOT-LOCK-FOR-UPDATE branch (lines 1444-
      *  1448).  Off-platform GnuCOBOL comments out EXEC CICS READ
      *  FILE UPDATE (lines 1427-1436) and EXEC CICS REWRITE (lines
      *  1477-1483) -- the precompiler substitutes CONTINUE for
      *  both -- but the IF guards on lines 1441 and 1488 remain
      *  live.  Pre-setting WS-RESP-CD=14 (DFHRESP value DUPREC,
      *  per DFHBMSCA.cpy line 225) makes the line-1441 IF EQUAL
      *  TO DFHRESP(NORMAL) FALSE, triggering the ELSE branch:
      *
      *    SET INPUT-ERROR                    TO TRUE  (line 1445)
      *    IF WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF                                      
      *        SET COULD-NOT-LOCK-FOR-UPDATE  TO TRUE  (line 1447)
      *    GO TO 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING-EXIT             (line 1449)
      *
      *  GO TO short-circuits before the 9300-CHECK-CHANGE-IN-REC
      *  PERFORM and the second EXEC CICS REWRITE -- this is the
      *  documented DUPREC conflict path per QA Phase 3.5 expect-
      *  ation.  Off-platform expression of the conflict scenario
      *  where another transaction holds the record lock; CICS
      *  returns DUPREC (14) on READ FILE UPDATE for an already-
      *  locked VSAM cluster.  COULD-NOT-LOCK-FOR-UPDATE's 88-VAL
      *  is the user-visible diagnostic message MOVE'd to CCARD-
      *  ERROR-MSG by 0000-MAIN's downstream RETURN flow.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    INPUT-ERROR  - SET TRUE line 1445 (88 VALUE '1' line 55).
      *    COULD-NOT-LOCK-FOR-UPDATE - SET TRUE line 1447 (88 VALUE
      *                  'Could not lock record for update' line 206).
      *                  WS-RETURN-MSG ends up holding that 32-byte
      *                  literal, space-padded to PIC X(75).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDUPC 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING DUPREC lock conflict'
            MOVE '0500024453765740' TO CC-CARD-NUM
            MOVE 14                 TO WS-RESP-CD
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING THRU 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING-EXIT
            EXPECT INPUT-ERROR TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT COULD-NOT-LOCK-FOR-UPDATE TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC9 -- 9300-CHECK-CHANGE-IN-REC detects concurrent change
      *
      *  Drives 9300-CHECK-CHANGE-IN-REC (production lines 1497-
      *  1521) along the DATA-WAS-CHANGED-BEFORE-UPDATE branch
      *  (line 1512).  This paragraph compares the current CARD-
      *  RECORD fields (CARD-CVV-CD, CARD-EMBOSSED-NAME, CARD-
      *  EXPIRAION-DATE substrings, CARD-ACTIVE-STATUS) against
      *  the CCUP-OLD-* snapshot fields.  When ANY mismatch is
      *  detected, the production sets DATA-WAS-CHANGED-BEFORE-
      *  UPDATE TRUE and refreshes the CCUP-OLD-* snapshot, then
      *  GO TO 9200-WRITE-PROCESSING-EXIT (paragraph-out).  The
      *  88-level VALUE is 'Record changed by some one else.
      *  Please review' (line 208).
      *
      *  Test setup deliberately supplies CARD-CVV-CD=001 (in
      *  CARD-RECORD via INITIALIZE then explicit MOVE) but
      *  CCUP-OLD-CVV-CD=999, so the line-1504 EQUAL test FAILS
      *  on the first AND-clause and the ELSE branch fires.
      *
      *  Off-platform expression of QA Phase 3.5 conflict-detection
      *  expectation; companion to TC8 (which exercises the lock
      *  conflict at the READ-UPDATE boundary).  Together they
      *  cover the two distinct concurrency-failure modes 9200
      *  must distinguish.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    DATA-WAS-CHANGED-BEFORE-UPDATE - SET TRUE line 1512
      *      (88 VALUE 'Record changed by some one else. Please
      *      review' on line 208 of WS-RETURN-MSG group).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COCRDUPC 9300-CHECK-CHANGE-IN-REC detects change'
            MOVE '001' TO CARD-CVV-CD
            MOVE '999' TO CCUP-OLD-CVV-CD
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM 9300-CHECK-CHANGE-IN-REC
                THRU 9300-CHECK-CHANGE-IN-REC-EXIT
            EXPECT DATA-WAS-CHANGED-BEFORE-UPDATE TO BE TRUE
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COCRDUPC CARD UPDATE TRANSACTION
      ******************************************************************
